{"name":"Yuzukoshō","hex":"#d4de49","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Yuzu koshō","blocks":[{"text":"Yuzu koshō  is a type of Japanese seasoning. It is a paste made from chili peppers, yuzu peel and salt, which is then allowed to ferment. It is usually used as a condiment for nabemono dishes, miso soup, and sashimi. The most famous types of yuzu koshō come from Kyushu, where it is a local specialty."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Yuzukosyou.jpg/330px-Yuzukosyou.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yuzu_kosh%C5%8D"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Chicken_breast_with_yuzu_kosho%2C_garlic%2C_olive_oil%2C_salt%2C_and_pepper_-_Massachusetts.jpg/500px-Chicken_breast_with_yuzu_kosho%2C_garlic%2C_olive_oil%2C_salt%2C_and_pepper_-_Massachusetts.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Chicken_breast_with_yuzu_kosho%2C_garlic%2C_olive_oil%2C_salt%2C_and_pepper_-_Massachusetts.jpg/1280px-Chicken_breast_with_yuzu_kosho%2C_garlic%2C_olive_oil%2C_salt%2C_and_pepper_-_Massachusetts.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Chicken_breast_with_yuzu_kosho%2C_garlic%2C_olive_oil%2C_salt%2C_and_pepper_-_Massachusetts.jpg/500px-Chicken_breast_with_yuzu_kosho%2C_garlic%2C_olive_oil%2C_salt%2C_and_pepper_-_Massachusetts.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Chicken breast with yuzu koshō","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChicken_breast_with_yuzu_kosho%2C_garlic%2C_olive_oil%2C_salt%2C_and_pepper_-_Massachusetts.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Smoked_herring_on_rotini%2C_with_olive_oil_and_yuzu_kosho_-_Massach